  "budget_literals_why": "Phase 36 part 2: a budget's value as written in culprit.yaml. The two YAML readers (Go's yaml.v3, YAML 1.2; Python's PyYAML, YAML 1.1) read some forms as different numbers or as strings, so both refuse every form but plain decimal digits, unquoted. The Go loader, culprit_model and the API's manifest model each refuse every case here marked refused, with this reason.",
  "budget_literals": [
    {
      "literal": "300",
      "plain": true,
      "refused": false
    },
    {
      "literal": "1",
      "plain": true,
      "refused": false
    },
    {
      "literal": "60000",
      "plain": true,
      "refused": false
    },
    {
      "literal": "1e3",
      "plain": true,
      "refused": true,
      "reason": "a budget is written as plain decimal digits, and this value is not",
      "why": "YAML 1.2 reads 1000; YAML 1.1 a string"
    },
    {
      "literal": "0o454",
      "plain": true,
      "refused": true,
      "reason": "a budget is written as plain decimal digits, and this value is not",
      "why": "YAML 1.2 reads octal 300; YAML 1.1 a string"
    },
    {
      "literal": "0454",
      "plain": true,
